  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nThe current algorithm uses an exhaustive search over possible functions to minimize the overlap integral. This approach is computationally expensive and may converge slowly. The central idea is to use a mathematical optimization framework with adaptive search controlling to more efficiently explore the function space. This involves reformulating the problem using a smooth function approximation with Bezier control points, adjusting hyperparameters adaptively based on performance metrics, introducing early termination heuristics, and integrating gradient-based polishing. The algorithm is designed to automatically adapt its search strategy while maintaining mathematically rigorous evaluations.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n- Objective: Minimize C5 = max_k \u222b[h(x)(1-h(x+k))]dx\n- Representation: Use Bezier control points p\u2080, p\u2081, ..., p_m (m determines resolution) to construct h(x) via the Bernstein basis\n- Constraints: \u222bh(x)dx=1 and 0\u2264h(x)\u22641 for all x\n- Relaxation: Solve a projected gradient problem with adaptive constraint enforcement\n- Termination: Track best fitness across function evaluations\n\n3. Detailed implementation:\na. Initialization:\n- Use provided parent as initial solution\n- Derive control points from parent via interpolation\n- Compute initial C5 score using autocorrelation\n\nb. Core optimization loop:\n1. Initialize stochastic gradient descent (SGD) parameters (lr=0.1, weight_decay=0.001)\n2. For iteration in range(max_iter):\n   i. Sample candidate control points \u03b8 from current \u03b8 + N(0, std)\n   ii. Project \u03b8 to [0,1]^m\u00d7[280,400] for feasibility\n   iii. Adjust std based on recent fitness improvement (std_cooling_factor=0.99)\n   iv. Compute C5 using:\n      - h(x) = \u03a3 B_i(x/2)(p_i)\n      - Correlation via Fourier transform with clipping\n   v. Update \u03b8 if new C5 improves by margin of \u22651e-4\n   vi. Apply constrained optimization via projected gradients\n   vii. Check time-based early termination (Budget=1300s)\n   viii. If stuck in local optimum, restart with perturbation\n\n4. Search space and parameters:\n- Control points (m=15): \u03b8 \u2208 [0,1]^{3*n_points}\n- Learning rate: adaptive between 0.001-0.1\n- Cooling schedules: exponential decrease in exploration\n- Population size: dynamically adjusts between 10-50 individuals\n- Termination triggers:\n   \u2022 Plateau detection (no improvement >10^6 iterations)\n   \u2022 Diminishing gradient size\n   \u2022 Time budget\n\n5. Progress tracking:\n- Maintain historical log: {iteration, best_score, \u2207magnitude, std}\n- Use Pareto fronts for adaptive parameter tuning\n- Monitor convergence rate with exponential smoothing of improvement signals\n\n6. Fallback mechanism:\n- Preserve initial parent solution\n- If optimization exceeds time budget, return best candidate found",
